  "section": "Movie Facts # 7 of 10",
  "description": "George Lucas screened an early cut of the film for his friends, among them directors Brian De Palma, John Milius, and Steven Spielberg. Alan Ladd, Jr. and the rest of 20th Century Fox loved what Lucas had wrought, which stunned the usually studio-phobic director. Although ongoing delays increased the film's budget from $8 million to $11 million, Star Wars was still the least expensive of the original trilogy. To everyone's surprise and delight, it would end up becoming the most successful motion picture of all time before the year was out."
